WEBVTT

00:17.017 --> 00:18.977
What? Hey! Stop!

00:25.066 --> 00:27.152
Let me see Mr. En!

01:56.032 --> 01:57.951
THE BEGINNING

02:02.622 --> 02:03.957
Caiman...

02:08.878 --> 02:09.838
Hey there.

02:10.505 --> 02:12.257
How are you feeling?

02:12.757 --> 02:14.425
Okay, I guess.

02:16.177 --> 02:19.347
I heard from Noi.
You're close to death, aren't you?

02:19.430 --> 02:21.349
You are so blunt, you know?

02:22.433 --> 02:23.518
Yes.

02:23.601 --> 02:28.273
I only hang on because I'm getting
Noi's smoke drip-fed like this.

02:30.400 --> 02:32.735
I know it's not the best time, but...

02:39.325 --> 02:42.745
- Boss, it's Fujita.
- Got it.

02:43.580 --> 02:45.248
What happened, Fujita?

02:46.958 --> 02:48.209
Ebisu...

02:50.170 --> 02:52.755
Ebisu is dead.

02:52.839 --> 02:55.091
Okay. And?

02:56.426 --> 03:01.014
Well... so, you know...

03:01.598 --> 03:03.766
We could use Kikurage...

03:04.601 --> 03:07.353
With Kikurage's magic...

03:08.479 --> 03:12.108
Fujita. Kikurage isn't my pet.

03:12.192 --> 03:13.902
She's a member of the family.

03:13.985 --> 03:15.904
IS IT TIME TO EAT?
GIVE ME FOOD, PLEASE.

03:15.987 --> 03:19.908
See? Kikurage is saying
it's just as I said.

03:19.991 --> 03:23.119
As proof, I've never given her an order.

03:23.995 --> 03:26.164
I took advantage of her nature, but...

03:26.247 --> 03:31.169
Then what am I supposed to do?
I want to bring Ebisu back to life.

03:31.794 --> 03:34.589
That depends completely
on Kikurage's feelings.

03:34.672 --> 03:35.673
And, by the way,

03:36.841 --> 03:42.180
if you try to force her to use her magic,
something terrifying will happen.

03:42.263 --> 03:44.807
What? Something terrifying?

03:46.267 --> 03:48.770
IT'S ABOUT TIME FOR MY PATROL.

03:48.853 --> 03:52.190
I guess it's best
to take advantage of her nature.

03:52.273 --> 03:57.195
I think she feels like reviving people
when there's a corpse nearby.

03:57.278 --> 04:01.199
She was close enough to Ebisu
to sleep with her.

04:01.783 --> 04:03.201
LET'S START WITH THIS ROOM...

04:04.786 --> 04:06.037
ALL CLEAR.

04:07.914 --> 04:09.707
Kikurage.

04:10.625 --> 04:12.460
Come here.

04:13.044 --> 04:14.462
Kikurage.

04:15.004 --> 04:16.965
THAT...

04:17.048 --> 04:18.716
Kikurage...

04:19.175 --> 04:20.969
...STINKS OF DEATH!

04:21.052 --> 04:23.680
Kikurage, wait!

04:24.931 --> 04:26.599
THAT WAS VERY UNPLEASANT.

04:26.683 --> 04:31.229
You know, I checked the head,
and there's definitely something wrong.

04:31.312 --> 04:34.857
The spikes on the head
were carefully cut off, and besides...

04:35.441 --> 04:36.484
Look.

04:36.567 --> 04:39.570
It looks like someone dissected it.

04:41.072 --> 04:42.240
I see.

04:42.824 --> 04:44.409
It's the head from back then.

04:44.492 --> 04:47.328
Oh, that's the one I severed, right?

04:47.412 --> 04:50.665
It does look like a head
my hammer knocked off.

04:51.332 --> 04:55.378
If that's the case,
why was this in that place?

04:56.004 --> 05:00.133
I don't know, but I saw it.

05:00.216 --> 05:03.177
Caiman doesn't have a lizard face anymore.

05:03.261 --> 05:04.470
- What?
- What?

05:04.971 --> 05:06.889
Is that true?

05:06.973 --> 05:08.308
What's that?

05:08.391 --> 05:09.684
Hey, wait!

05:11.978 --> 05:14.939
If that lizard guy's face
is back to normal,

05:15.023 --> 05:17.775
then Ebisu had cast magic on him.

05:18.776 --> 05:20.028
Did you kill her?

05:20.111 --> 05:23.948
No, I didn't!
I just want Kikurage to revive her.

05:24.032 --> 05:28.244
Even if you revive her, I wonder
if the Devil tumor in her head is okay.

05:28.328 --> 05:30.371
Fujita, have him take a look.

05:30.455 --> 05:32.957
He may not mean well,
but his skills are solid.

05:35.793 --> 05:36.919
Her hair!

05:37.003 --> 05:39.130
You taped it up yourself, didn't you?

05:39.714 --> 05:42.133
Yeah, it looks like it's okay.

05:42.216 --> 05:47.305
Before you revive her and stuff,
let Noi fix the damage to the body.

05:47.388 --> 05:48.806
I'll do that.

05:49.807 --> 05:55.104
Still, everyone's so indifferent
about Ebisu's death.

05:55.605 --> 05:59.609
Would they react the same way if I died?

06:00.109 --> 06:02.028
Kikurage! Hey!

06:02.111 --> 06:04.989
Don't run away! Isn't Ebisu your friend?!

06:06.324 --> 06:08.242
What are you doing, you idiot?!

06:08.326 --> 06:10.745
My mushroom almost snapped!
You trying to kill me?!

06:10.828 --> 06:13.039
Chota.

06:14.248 --> 06:16.959
Sorry, I didn't realize
it was you, Fujita.

06:17.043 --> 06:19.253
After all, I can't see, you know?

06:19.337 --> 06:20.922
That must be tough.

06:21.005 --> 06:25.635
But wouldn't it be easy for you to turn
yourself back to normal with your magic?

06:25.718 --> 06:28.805
That's true, but you know, this mushroom...

06:28.888 --> 06:32.350
It smells like En, so I like it.

06:32.433 --> 06:34.060
Is that so?

06:35.269 --> 06:37.563
Don't you smell something weird?

06:37.647 --> 06:40.191
Well, actually...

06:40.942 --> 06:43.319
I see. So Ebisu is...

06:43.403 --> 06:47.782
That's true! Ebisu doesn't have much luck.

06:47.865 --> 06:50.326
- She doesn't have much hair now either.
- Here it is!

06:51.077 --> 06:53.162
I got this from a Devil long ago.

06:53.246 --> 06:58.334
It seems that if you wear this hairpin,
you can always be smiling and happy.

06:58.418 --> 07:01.337
I'll put it on her... Done.

07:02.255 --> 07:04.674
Good for you, Ebisu.

07:07.677 --> 07:11.013
Now, where did Kikurage go?

07:12.181 --> 07:13.599
It's Noi!

07:13.683 --> 07:15.852
Noi!

07:15.935 --> 07:20.481
All right, come at me from anywhere!

07:39.083 --> 07:42.086
Fujita! Are you okay?

07:42.837 --> 07:47.300
I'm sorry. I was so into my training
that I didn't notice you.

07:48.259 --> 07:50.678
What happened? Where's Ebisu?

07:53.347 --> 07:54.682
Did you kill her?

07:54.765 --> 07:56.559
I didn't!

07:56.642 --> 07:58.686
- I just need to fix her, right?
- What?

08:03.316 --> 08:05.693
Hey, wait a minute!

08:05.776 --> 08:09.197
You just healed her
while the hairpin was inside her head.

08:09.280 --> 08:12.909
Really? Well, just come again
if something's wrong with her.

08:12.992 --> 08:14.202
I'll heal her.

08:14.911 --> 08:16.829
Will she be okay?

08:16.913 --> 08:18.706
But the smell of rot is gone.

08:19.415 --> 08:22.293
It's good that you're pretty now, Ebisu.

08:23.419 --> 08:25.087
So heavy...

08:25.171 --> 08:27.882
I'm at my limit.

08:29.175 --> 08:30.593
There you are, Kikurage.

08:32.428 --> 08:33.679
PUNCH!

08:34.430 --> 08:36.432
DID YOU DIE AGAIN?

08:37.934 --> 08:39.685
LET'S PLAY SOME MORE.

08:41.437 --> 08:43.814
PUNCH!

08:44.815 --> 08:46.609
DID YOU DIE AGAIN?

08:46.943 --> 08:48.945
THIS WILL MAKE YOU FEEL BETTER.

08:51.030 --> 08:53.407
Stop it!

08:53.491 --> 08:55.743
Don't waste magic on that!

08:55.826 --> 09:01.707
Look, it's a corpse.
Bring it back to life, quick!

09:08.714 --> 09:12.552
So that was the terrifying thing.

09:13.052 --> 09:14.720
EBISU

09:15.763 --> 09:20.977
In the end, I wasn't able
to revive Ebisu today.

09:21.644 --> 09:23.938
I'll try again tomorrow.

09:29.569 --> 09:31.821
HEY, MISS. ARE YOU SLEEPING?

09:32.822 --> 09:35.575
WE HAVE A DEAL. YOU ALWAYS
GIVE ME A SNACK AT THIS TIME.

09:35.825 --> 09:39.662
WAKE UP, MISS!
IT'S TIME FOR MY SNACK!

09:46.168 --> 09:47.920
NOW, GIVE ME A SNACK.

09:55.177 --> 09:57.096
Just what on earth

09:58.889 --> 10:00.099
are you?

10:07.398 --> 10:10.401
This dream again. Damn it.

10:10.484 --> 10:12.737
Could it be that I'm scared?

10:13.946 --> 10:16.866
Is the Cross-Eyes boss still alive?

10:17.408 --> 10:19.994
If I could use Nikaido's magic...

10:22.079 --> 10:24.040
Hydration.

10:24.832 --> 10:26.000
Ebisu.

10:27.335 --> 10:31.088
I heard you got a new mask.
It looks good on you.

10:31.172 --> 10:32.757
I can't actually see it, though.

10:35.217 --> 10:38.721
Looks like the hairpin I gave her
is still inside her head,

10:38.804 --> 10:41.349
and that made her a little off again.

10:41.432 --> 10:42.933
I'm laughing my ass off.

10:46.687 --> 10:51.400
Ever since I became a mushroom,
I feel at ease in dark forests like this.

10:52.151 --> 10:55.404
Let's see the horoscope
for Gemini Sorcerers this month.

10:55.488 --> 10:56.781
Gemini is my sign!

10:56.864 --> 10:58.407
So-so.

10:58.491 --> 11:01.619
Something may happen
that makes you fall even harder

11:01.702 --> 11:03.788
for your long-time one-sided crush.

11:03.871 --> 11:05.623
I'm looking forward to that.

11:05.706 --> 11:06.707
Now to Capricorns.

11:06.791 --> 11:08.709
But only "so-so"?

11:08.793 --> 11:10.294
Oh, that's En.

11:10.378 --> 11:11.671
Bad.

11:11.754 --> 11:15.299
Still, problems left unsolved in the past
are likely to be settled.

11:15.383 --> 11:18.177
She said it's "bad." Poor En.

11:18.260 --> 11:19.637
Next up, Pisces.

11:19.720 --> 11:21.514
But I'm a little worried.

11:21.597 --> 11:22.682
Good.

11:22.765 --> 11:25.685
This horoscope is usually spot on.

11:26.268 --> 11:28.896
Good work. Would you like
something to drink?

11:28.979 --> 11:30.189
Yes, please!

11:30.272 --> 11:31.732
TERMITE EXTERMINATION

11:31.816 --> 11:33.234
I'm so tired.

11:33.776 --> 11:36.070
It doesn't cost much upfront,

11:36.153 --> 11:39.198
but exterminating termites
with liquid poison is hard.

11:41.158 --> 11:44.412
But I need money to cover
Tetsujo's and Ton's treatment.

11:44.495 --> 11:46.706
Big bro! Big bro Dokuga!

11:46.789 --> 11:49.041
You've got a drink! Give me a sip of--

11:49.125 --> 11:50.710
Stop it. You'll die.

11:50.793 --> 11:53.379
How much did you make today?

11:53.462 --> 11:55.589
Six hundred nicks from three houses.

11:55.673 --> 11:58.843
I made 800 nicks as a waitress.

11:58.926 --> 12:00.720
Really? I see...

12:03.180 --> 12:04.223
Dokuga.

12:04.306 --> 12:06.642
I talked it over with Ushishimada,

12:06.726 --> 12:09.770
and I think we've got no choice
but to pawn this.

12:09.854 --> 12:12.732
This is all the both of us
could earn today.

12:14.316 --> 12:19.113
There aren't any decent jobs
for people like us who can't use magic.

12:19.196 --> 12:20.656
It's just as he says.

12:20.740 --> 12:22.742
To save Tetsujo and Ton,

12:22.825 --> 12:26.245
we need to get some A-rank smoke
as soon as possible.

12:28.831 --> 12:30.624
We can't pawn this knife.

12:30.708 --> 12:32.710
Dokuga! Why not?

12:32.793 --> 12:36.172
Are you saying you don't care
if Tetsujo and Ton die?

12:36.255 --> 12:39.258
For starters,
you're hiding something from us--

12:40.718 --> 12:41.844
- Hey!
- Listen up.

12:41.927 --> 12:45.473
This is something
I got directly from the boss.

12:45.556 --> 12:47.475
I'll return it to him myself.

12:48.392 --> 12:51.479
I'll also get back
everything we've pawned until now.

12:51.562 --> 12:53.814
I'll do something about the money.

12:53.898 --> 12:55.900
If you understand, just shut up.

12:56.567 --> 12:58.486
Okay, I get it.

12:58.569 --> 13:00.070
I get it.

13:01.614 --> 13:02.865
Hey, Dokuga!

13:05.451 --> 13:07.828
CROSS-EYE EXPEDITION

13:10.539 --> 13:16.128
Shaitan. An organization
of the few heal-and-repair-type Sorcerers.

13:17.046 --> 13:21.133
They're the ones driving up the price
of healing-type smoke.

13:22.176 --> 13:24.637
The heavy security and bodyguards

13:24.720 --> 13:26.639
make it hard to break in.

13:26.722 --> 13:27.640
However...

13:29.433 --> 13:32.144
Every day, they invite women
and throw parties.

13:32.728 --> 13:34.647
All right, let's have fun!

13:38.234 --> 13:41.570
This booze is great. Drink up!

13:41.654 --> 13:45.032
There's a lot more in that jar too.

13:45.991 --> 13:49.245
They're having another party
downstairs today?

13:49.328 --> 13:51.914
We wanna have some fun
once in a while too.

13:53.415 --> 13:55.167
Would you like some fruit?

14:15.062 --> 14:19.775
Until now, any Cross-Eye who stood out
was eliminated by En.

14:20.901 --> 14:24.321
That's why we waited quietly
for the boss to return.

14:24.822 --> 14:25.698
But not anymore.

14:25.781 --> 14:27.616
Die!

14:31.287 --> 14:33.706
A murder without magic.

14:34.415 --> 14:38.002
En will definitely hear about this.

14:40.796 --> 14:44.008
Boss. Where are you now?

14:48.262 --> 14:49.680
Where am I?

14:51.682 --> 14:54.935
Who are you?

14:55.644 --> 14:58.856
The name's Aikawa. Nice to meet you.

14:58.939 --> 15:00.941
BIG BANDAGE MASK
SAFE AND SECURE

15:01.025 --> 15:04.695
I'm glad I bought big-sized bandage masks.

15:06.280 --> 15:08.407
All right, I'm doing it.

15:17.541 --> 15:20.419
Thank you.
The stinging has subsided a little.

15:20.502 --> 15:24.423
What's your name?
And why do you look like that?

15:24.506 --> 15:26.258
I'm Asu...

15:26.342 --> 15:28.427
No. I'm Kawajiri.

15:29.011 --> 15:30.471
Don't you remember?

15:30.554 --> 15:33.849
The Devil you met
in the church basement at En's mansion.

15:35.017 --> 15:36.310
What do you mean?

15:36.393 --> 15:40.147
Aren't you the man named Caiman?

15:40.230 --> 15:43.317
The friend of Nikaido's
who was in the Hole.

15:43.400 --> 15:46.946
Nikaido? I don't know anyone by that name.

15:48.113 --> 15:51.075
It seems I have mistaken you
for someone else.

15:51.575 --> 15:54.954
Anyway, thanks for your help.
I'm going now.

15:56.372 --> 15:58.123
Going? Hey, wait!

16:04.213 --> 16:06.256
It's time to work, you two.

16:07.132 --> 16:09.385
So the Cross-Eyes are on the move again?

16:09.885 --> 16:10.844
Yeah.

16:10.928 --> 16:15.557
Everyone who was at a shop
called "Shaitan" in Devas was slaughtered.

16:16.058 --> 16:20.604
The footprints suggest there's
only one culprit, and they used a blade.

16:21.105 --> 16:26.360
It might be the Cross-Eyes' boss.
Make sure you finish him!

16:29.571 --> 16:33.993
And so, we're off to work, Mr. Kasukabe.

16:34.076 --> 16:36.578
Be a good boy, kid.

16:36.662 --> 16:41.000
Shin, I'd like to meet a Devil.
How do I make that happen?

16:41.083 --> 16:45.587
I heard there's a room in the mansion
to summon Devils.

16:45.671 --> 16:47.256
But be careful with that.

16:47.339 --> 16:49.883
Got it. I'll look for it.

16:53.470 --> 16:55.973
What am I so anxious about?

16:56.473 --> 17:01.645
To think I'd send Shin and Noi
without being sure it was the Cross-Eyes.

17:02.855 --> 17:06.275
However, what is this uneasiness?

17:06.358 --> 17:08.652
En, let's have some tea!

17:09.653 --> 17:11.030
Chota.

17:13.240 --> 17:16.493
En, what are you
planning to do with Nikaido?

17:16.577 --> 17:19.788
She's going to die
if you leave her like this.

17:20.289 --> 17:24.668
For some reason,
Nikaido won't use her magic at all.

17:25.377 --> 17:29.173
Until now, I respected her will
and watched over her.

17:29.798 --> 17:31.175
But I'm at my limit.

17:32.426 --> 17:34.762
I'll make her use magic, no matter what.

17:34.845 --> 17:37.181
Even if I have to be a bit rough.

17:38.265 --> 17:41.351
Is the Cross-Eyes' boss really dead?

17:41.435 --> 17:43.187
I must confirm that.

17:43.687 --> 17:48.317
Six years ago,
I blew smoke at him. And then...

17:48.400 --> 17:51.361
The town of Mastema was destroyed.

17:51.862 --> 17:55.824
No one could survive that
without turning into a mushroom.

17:55.908 --> 17:59.036
But I saw it.

17:59.119 --> 18:03.832
The shadow of a headless man
crawling out of the mushrooms.

18:09.588 --> 18:11.840
- Where are we?
- En's mansion.

18:11.924 --> 18:14.551
Is this your magic?

18:15.719 --> 18:18.555
Nikaido is up ahead. Let's go.

18:20.140 --> 18:21.183
Damn it.

18:22.768 --> 18:26.855
Still, aren't you a great Sorcerer?

18:26.939 --> 18:30.067
Being able to go anywhere you want,
I envy you!

18:30.692 --> 18:32.820
What kind of magic do you use?

18:33.904 --> 18:38.408
Well... I can't tell someone I just met.

18:39.827 --> 18:40.911
Nikaido.

18:42.913 --> 18:43.831
Who are you?

18:43.914 --> 18:47.126
Nikaido! It's me, Asu.

18:47.209 --> 18:48.210
Asu?

18:48.293 --> 18:52.881
Chidaruma turned me back into a Sorcerer,
and now I look like this.

18:53.465 --> 18:56.510
So that's what happened to you, Asu.

18:56.593 --> 18:59.888
Don't tell me Chidaruma did this
because you helped me.

18:59.972 --> 19:00.889
It's okay.

19:00.973 --> 19:04.143
After all, you saved me before.

19:04.226 --> 19:06.395
More importantly, your body...

19:07.271 --> 19:09.648
It's because I'm rejecting
the contract with En.

19:10.232 --> 19:12.234
I'm still able to stay sane,

19:13.235 --> 19:16.405
but I think I'm at my limit.

19:16.989 --> 19:20.409
Anyway, let's run away together.
My magic can handle it.

19:21.910 --> 19:23.912
- Who is he?
- Right.

19:23.996 --> 19:26.957
- That guy is...
- I'm Aikawa.

19:27.040 --> 19:30.294
I have nothing to do with this,
but he brought me here.

19:30.794 --> 19:32.045
That voice...

19:32.129 --> 19:35.799
I'm sorry, could you take off that mask
and show me your face?

19:35.883 --> 19:38.051
What? Why?

19:38.135 --> 19:41.305
Why can't you take it off?
It's not a big deal, is it?

19:41.388 --> 19:42.723
Nikaido?

19:42.806 --> 19:45.642
Good grief. I'm gonna get out of here.

19:46.226 --> 19:47.477
Caiman!

19:50.230 --> 19:52.608
I don't know who that is.

19:52.691 --> 19:54.735
If you don't take off your mask...

20:01.033 --> 20:02.492
Stop it!

20:07.289 --> 20:09.291
See? You should stop--

20:10.459 --> 20:11.627
Damn it...

20:13.587 --> 20:14.630
Gotcha!

20:16.632 --> 20:18.050
Nikaido!

20:25.140 --> 20:26.600
Caiman...

20:31.939 --> 20:33.899
Are you happy now?

20:35.984 --> 20:39.321
Jeez, you really are a violent girl.

20:39.988 --> 20:41.990
Caiman...

20:46.995 --> 20:48.372
Goodbye.

21:02.719 --> 21:04.012
Nikaido.

21:04.680 --> 21:07.474
Was that man Caiman after all?

21:08.058 --> 21:09.184
I don't know.

21:10.227 --> 21:11.895
Should we go after him?

21:12.396 --> 21:13.438
Yeah.

21:18.652 --> 21:20.821
Nikaido, Nikai...

21:22.572 --> 21:24.449
Damn, the drip-feed!

21:24.533 --> 21:26.118
Nikaido!

21:28.912 --> 21:31.832
I'm getting headaches again.

21:37.921 --> 21:39.840
I found him.

21:43.051 --> 21:46.346
Since you were revived,
you've been laughing nonstop.

21:47.222 --> 21:50.434
Don't laugh when we go to Mr. En's place.

21:50.934 --> 21:55.355
After all, we're going to ask him
to let you stay at the mansion.

21:56.148 --> 21:59.484
You're all on your own now.
Do you understand?

22:10.495 --> 22:11.455
You idiot!

22:15.459 --> 22:16.376
What is this?

22:16.960 --> 22:17.878
Whoa!

22:20.380 --> 22:24.301
What's happening?
This feeling is just like...

22:32.893 --> 22:35.729
Today, I'll definitely make Nikaido
use her magic.

22:35.812 --> 22:37.689
I can't hold back anymore.

22:38.899 --> 22:40.067
Kikurage.

22:40.150 --> 22:41.234
Come here.

22:42.235 --> 22:43.070
Kikurage?

22:44.154 --> 22:45.614
The security device...

22:45.697 --> 22:47.908
And she's terrified.

22:49.409 --> 22:51.828
What is this feeling? I feel sick.

22:51.912 --> 22:53.580
DEFORMED REUNION

23:06.176 --> 23:07.469
You...

23:13.558 --> 23:14.976
As I thought.

23:15.560 --> 23:17.729
You're alive!

23:21.525 --> 23:22.359
What?

23:22.442 --> 23:24.736
Take care of Kikurage, Chota.

23:24.820 --> 23:26.571
En!

23:29.449 --> 23:35.664
En!

23:41.169 --> 23:43.338
It's the same as six years ago.

23:43.422 --> 23:46.425
I'm getting dizzy.
My entire body aches and throbs.

23:47.259 --> 23:48.802
The fight will be over in an instant.

24:03.024 --> 24:05.402
I'll end this with my own hands.

24:13.785 --> 24:16.872
Blow out smoke, En!

24:34.931 --> 24:36.349
En!

24:36.433 --> 24:39.144
How long is this mushroom going to fly?

24:40.437 --> 24:41.855
I turned back to normal?

24:43.607 --> 24:44.608
Why?

24:46.735 --> 24:50.363
No way... That can't be...

24:50.447 --> 24:54.367
En!

24:56.119 --> 24:58.371
A headless man. That must be...

26:41.641 --> 26:42.934
THE END

26:43.018 --> 26:45.228
What we learned in Episode 7.

26:45.312 --> 26:47.188
Fujita's love for Ebisu is real.

26:47.272 --> 26:49.149
Chota's head is ever-changing.

26:49.232 --> 26:50.984
The boss's strength is overwhelming.

26:51.067 --> 26:52.110
En!

26:52.193 --> 26:56.072
What we'll learn in Episode 8
is still hidden in chaos.

26:56.156 --> 26:57.949
This is Dorohedoro.
